  "answer": "Both halves of this request have been filed before. PowerToys#47291 asks for a Power Display control for Windows' SDR content brightness when HDR is on. PowerToys#48784 and PowerToys#48422 ask for global shortcuts to raise and lower brightness and contrast. The shortcut tickets were marked as duplicates of PowerToys#47290, which tracks Keyboard Manager integration. That ticket wasn't in the results I was shown, so I haven't read it. PowerToys#48784 was reopened because it asks for built-in Power Display hotkeys, which is a different scope from #47290. I found no past ticket that asks for the SDR control and the shortcuts together. It also isn't clear whether any of these tickets cover volume shortcuts, an SDR shortcut, or the 'SDR Replaces Primary Slider' setting. Subscribe to and comment on those tickets rather than opening a new one. Link your working implementation and tests there, and tell the maintainers it covers both features. Until the feature ships, the SDR content brightness slider in Windows Settings > System > Display > HDR is the only way to change SDR brightness. Power Display's brightness slider changes the monitor's backlight."
